Fix a truthiness bypass bug in `scripts/fleet/archive-stale-sessions.ts`.

The parsing logic for `--source-filter` uses JS truthiness: `if (arg === "--source-filter" && argv[i + 1])`. If the argument is a whitespace-only string (`"   "`), it is truthy and accepted, which later bypasses the deny-by-default gate for `--apply` mode.

Change the logic to explicitly check for a non-empty, non-whitespace string, throwing an error otherwise.

Before:
```typescript
    } else if (arg === "--source-filter" && argv[i + 1]) {
      sourceFilter = argv[++i];
    } else if (arg === "--repo" && argv[i + 1]) {
```
After:
```typescript
    } else if (arg === "--source-filter") {
      const value = argv[++i];
      if (value === undefined || value.trim().length === 0) {
        throw new Error("--source-filter requires a non-empty value");
      }
      sourceFilter = value;
    } else if (arg === "--repo" && argv[i + 1]) {
```

Add two new tests to `scripts/fleet/archive-stale-sessions.test.ts` to cover this behavior:
1. `--apply with whitespace-only --source-filter is denied`
2. `--apply with empty --source-filter is denied`

Acceptance criteria:
- Whitespace-only or empty `--source-filter` throws an error.
- New tests are added and pass.
- You may ONLY modify the files listed above. If a test file outside your boundary fails, you must make your source changes backward-compatible so the existing test passes unmodified. Do NOT rename, move, or delete any files outside your boundary.
